    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SITE FOR SALE\r\nCIRCA 1.9 ACRES\r\nAT BOOLYDUFF, INAGH,CO. CLARE\r\n\r\nFOR SALE SUBJECT TO PLANNING PERMISSION\r\nCONTAINED IN FOLIO CE64516F.\r\n\r\nVIEWINGS STRICTLY BY ADVANCE APPOINTMENT WITH SOLE AGENT\r\nSTREETS AHEAD PROPERTIES\r\nPROPERTY LICENCE NO 003178\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nStreets Ahead Properties are delighted to bring to the market this site circa 1.9 acres, contained in Folio CE64516F just off the R460.\r\n\r\nLocated on a rural road circa 9km from Inagh and circa 10km from Miltown Malbay. The property is located beside Eircode, V95 A392 *for directional purposes only*.   \r\n\r\nNestled in the peaceful countryside of Boolyduff, Inagh, County Clare, this attractive site enjoys a tranquil rural setting surrounded by rolling farmland and scenic natural beauty. The site offers an excellent opportunity to create a high-quality family home in a quiet location while remaining within easy reach of essential amenities. Its convenient location offers easy access to Inagh village, Ennis, Ennistymon and Lahinch, while also being close to the Wild Atlantic Way and the many attractions of County Clare and a 40 minute drive to Shannon International Airport.\r\n\r\nInagh is a small rural village in the west of County Clare, situated along the main road between Ennis and Miltown Malbay. The village is known for its strong agricultural traditions and its close-knit community, with farming playing an important role in the local economy.  Inagh lies near the scenic Cahercommaun Ring Fort and is within easy reach of the rugged landscapes of The Burren and Atlantic coastline.\r\n\r\nMiltown Malbay is a Market town on Ireland’s west coast, known for its strong tradition of Irish music and welcoming community spirit. Situated along the Wild Atlantic Way, it is just inland from the seaside of Spanish Point, with its beautiful beaches and Atlantic views nearby. The town is internationally famous for the Willie Clancy Summer School, a major annual festival celebrating traditional music, song and dance. With its local pubs hosting regular music sessions. It has shops, pubs, restaurants and local services."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Quiet location offering privacy and a peaceful rural environment.\r\n9 km from Inagh village and 10km from Miltown Malbay.\r\nClose to local amenities including schools, shops, GAA facilities and community services in Inagh.\r\nExcellent base for accessing the Wild Atlantic Way, the Burren and Shannon Airport.\r\nAll facilities close by.\r\nAttractive countryside setting with scenic views of the surrounding Clare landscape.\r\nApproximately 20 minutes from Ennis and Lahinch."
      }
    ],
